--- body ---
## Context

The primary checkout's `.env` (gitignored, last edited 2026-05-24) holds nine
inline values, six of them live credentials: `AGENT_GH_TOKEN`,
`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `HF_TOKEN`, `ZENODO_TOKEN`, `HAL_PASSWORD`,
`OPENAI_API_KEY` (plus `HAL_ID`, `AGENT_GIT_NAME`, `AGENT_GIT_EMAIL`).
Audit of 2026-09-24, value-equality booleans only, no value printed:

- Every inline value is a copy of a `~/.config/keys/` entry. `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
  equals `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_AEDIST@openrouter.env`; all others match their
  same-name entry. Deleting them loses nothing.
- **Ambient residency.** The harness `bash-env.sh` strict-parses every project
  `.env` and exports each unprotected name into every bash subprocess, so these
  credentials sit in the environment of every shell opened in this repo —
  what harness tracker 0942 set out to end.
- **Group-readable.** The file was mode 0664, group `untrusted-runner` (the
  sandbox user's primary group). Tightened to 0600 on 2026-09-24; the values
  were readable to that account before.
- **0679 did not land here.** It closed 2026-07-14 as "migration applied and
  verified", moving HF/Zenodo/HAL behind a `KEYS=` line. The primary `.env`
  predates it and still carries them inline, with no `KEYS=` line. The
  migration was probably applied to a worktree copy. `KEYS=` itself is gone
  from the harness since 2026-09-17 (harness 0945), so that route is closed.
- **Name drift.** The adapters read `OPENAI_API_KEY_AEDIST`,
  `QWEN_API_KEY_AEDIST`, `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,
  `TAVILY_API_KEY`; none of these is in `.env`, while `.env` carries
  `OPENAI_API_KEY` and `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` that the adapters may no longer
  read. Which runs currently work is unknown.
- History is clean: `.env` never committed; no secret-shaped string in
  `git log --all -p`.

## Approach

The repo policy (ticket 0240, `tests/test_secret_loading_policy.py`,
`experiments/common.mk` ENV POLICY) says source code reads keys only from its
environment and never opens key files; Make injects them via
`UV_RUN := uv run --project .. --env-file ../.env`. That contract can stay:
point `--env-file` at the keystore files instead of the project `.env`
(`uv run` accepts several `--env-file`), so each run gets exactly the
providers it needs, per invocation, and no shell carries them. Rename to the
keystore names (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY_AEDIST`, `OPENAI_API_KEY_AEDIST`, ...) or
map explicitly — decide and record in the commit.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `.env` holds no credential value (only non-secret settings, if any)
- [ ] A fresh `bash -c env` in the repo carries none of the names above
      (names-only probe)
- [ ] `UV_RUN` (and the `scripts/`, `src/aedist/*` docstrings that say
      `--env-file ../.env`) resolve from `~/.config/keys/`; ENV POLICY header in
      `experiments/acquire.mk` / `common.mk` rewritten
- [ ] Each adapter's key resolves: a names-only smoke (`aedist.smoke` or
      equivalent) per provider, no paid call needed beyond one per provider
- [ ] `tests/test_secret_loading_policy.py` updated to the new contract and
      still guarding against `load_dotenv` / hard-coded key paths in `src/`
- [ ] 0679's closing claim corrected by a log note here (not reopened)
- [ ] Decide on rotating `AGENT_GH_TOKEN` and `OPENAI_API_KEY` (group-readable
      to `untrusted-runner` until 2026-09-24); record the decision
- [ ] `make check` passes
